    "title": "The Bill Comes Due",
    "description": "A painterly Western fine art portrait steeped in shadow, superstition, and inevitability. Bathed in warm lamplight, the scene captures a moment when chance gives way to reckoning. Cards, coins, and whiskey frame a quiet realization—this is no longer a game of luck, but of consequence. Wayne Heim’s cinematic approach allows the weight of recognition to settle before anything moves, inviting viewers into a pause where fate finishes its accounting. © Wayne Heim",
