    "story": "Another crossing.\nClosing in.\nDaylight writes her closing hymn.\n\nMiles to go\nto reach the end.\n\nGod be willing,\nthis path less followed…\nleads us back\nto home again.",
    "notes": "This scene calls back to the golden age of Western painters—think Charles Russell’s trail stories, or the mentorship found in Frederic Remington’s lesser-known works. Here, Heim’s painterly process turns a moment of guidance and learning into a work of enduring art. The colt’s youthful energy, set against the steady presence of the riders, becomes a metaphor for the passing down of knowledge and the untamed promise of the West. Every brushstroke and highlight feels deliberate, pulling the viewer into the rhythm of the journey and the quiet legacy of life on the trail.",
