    "id": "i-8rsG6P9",
    "title": "Every Morning",
    "description": "In this haunting portrait of resilience, a woman kneels at a grave beneath the pale dawn, wrapped in the quiet resolve of frontier life. Wayne Heim’s painterly fine art photography captures the private sorrow and perseverance of the American West—where the morning sun demands forward motion, even as memory clings to what’s lost. A tribute to those who endured, and to the small, unspoken acts of mourning that shaped the world of the West. © Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "Frontier woman mourning at sunrise beside a wooden grave marker – Painterly Western Fine Art by Wayne Heim",
