    "title": "This Is the Hand — I Can Feel It",
    "description": "A painterly Western fine art portrait suspended between belief and consequence. Wayne Heim captures the fragile confidence of a man who still trusts in one last turn of fortune—where debt, regret, and hope collide at the table. The image resists closure, allowing superstition and self-assurance to coexist in the narrow space before reality asserts itself. © Wayne Heim",
